// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/claw/gates.t27 -- the TRI CLAW gate inventory: every CI gate in this repository, as data.
; Epic #9271. This file is the single source of truth the TRI CLAW service reads: the audit law
; below (claw_status) is lowered by `t27c gen-c` into gen/c/claw/gates.c, and the gate-topology
; workflow compiles a four-line harness around it that diffs NAMES against
; .github/workflows/*.yml on disk, so a workflow file cannot land without its row here in the
; same commit -- the same ratchet discipline scripts/ci/check_pr_branch_filters.py holds for
; merge-critical classification. The law lives here, not in the harness (owner rule 2026-10-13:
; everything new is .t27); the harness is machinery only.
; The extraction recipe (how NAMES/CLASSES/EVENTS are regenerated from the workflow files) lives in
; docs/claw/README.md; do not hand-edit rows, regenerate them.
; --
; Class rule, mechanically checkable from the workflow files:
; - G_SOFT (1): the workflow carries `continue-on-error` -- failure is reported, never fatal
;   (oracle-nightly, queen-doctor, rings-rust).
; - G_REPORTING (2): the workflow only merges, opens or files work -- its own failure gates no
;   merge (auto-merge-ready-prs merges ready PRs; queen-publish opens PRs from bee branches, and
;   the gates on those PRs are what gate). Same judgement, same two files, as the NOT_MERGE_CRITICAL
;   entries in scripts/ci/check_pr_branch_filters.py; stated here as data, not copied reasoning.
;   Measured 2026-10-12: both also carry push/dispatch triggers, so "schedule-only" would be false.
; - G_BLOCKING (0): everything else -- a failure can fail the run and so can block a merge.
; - An unknown name is G_UNKNOWN, never G_BLOCKING: a gate list that silently waves through a name
;   it does not know is not a gate list (fail-closed applies to the inventory reader in T2).
; EVENTS are the `on:` trigger keys of each workflow, comma-joined, as measured 2026-10-12; they
; are recorded data for the report, not a class rule -- the class rule above is the law.
; Snapshot: 69 workflows, 2026-10-25 (t27os-release, the dispatch-only T27 OS release leg, #12479; t27os landed in #12330). Census: 64 blocking + 3 soft + 2 reporting.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module ClawGates;

use claw::text;

/// A workflow class. G_UNKNOWN is deliberately far from the real classes so a
/// partial read cannot mistake it for a verdict.
pub const G_BLOCKING : u8 = 0;
pub const G_SOFT : u8 = 1;
pub const G_REPORTING : u8 = 2;
pub const G_UNKNOWN : u8 = 255;

/// Total workflow files in .github/workflows/ this inventory claims to cover.
/// T2 fails when the directory and this number disagree.
pub const COUNT : u32 = 69;

